ay.md\", \"score\": 1.0357}, {\"text\": \"Harnesses\\n\\nA harness is a way of running the agent loop. The prompt-agent harness lets Foundry run the loop.\\nThe langgraph harness would run the loop in our own container, hosted by Foundry. Both sit behind\\none HarnessAdapter contract and emit the same AgentEvent stream, so the frontend, traces and voice\\nwork with either.\", \"source\": \"architecture.md\", \"score\": 0.5}, {\"text\": \"Two things called AI Gateway\\n\\nThe project-level AI Gateway governs direct model calls. Foundry Agent Service does not route its\\ninternal inference through it. To route the agent's inference through your own Azure API Management\\ninstance you use bring your own model, which is a separate Admin-connected model connection. With\\nthat connection the agent's model is named connection-name/model-name.\", \"source\": \"gateway.md\", \"score\": 0.0667}]}", "status": "completed", "response_id": "caresp_0000", "agent_reference": {"type": "agent_reference", "name": "foundry-live-agent-hosted", "version": "2"}}, {"type": "message", "id": "msg_0009", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "output_text", "text": "Right now in S\u00e3o Paulo, it is **14:50 on Wednesday, 16 September 2026**.\n\nThe repository knowledge base says its **harnesses** are ways of running the agent loop:\n\n- The **prompt-agent harness** lets **Foundry run the loop**.\n- The **langgraph harness** would run the loop **in the project\u2019s own container**, hosted by Foundry.\n- Both sit behind the same **`HarnessAdapter` contract**.\n- Both emit the same **`AgentEvent` stream**, so the frontend, traces, and voice functionality work with either harness.", "annotations": [], "logprobs": []}], "status": "completed", "response_id": "caresp_0000", "agent_reference": {"type": "agent_reference", "name": "foundry-live-agent-hosted", "version": "2"}}], "created_at": 1789581030, "error": null, "incomplete_details": null, "instructions": null, "parallel_tool_calls": false